<title>USA: U.S. HEADLINE STOCKS - Issues to Watch - Nov 5.</title>
<headline>U.S. HEADLINE STOCKS - Issues to Watch - Nov 5.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stocks to watch this morning:</p>
<p>-- Apogee Inc said some of its unit's medicare billings were being reviewed by the U.S. Department of Health and Human Services and the Departement of Justice.</p>
<p>Apogee shares closed at 6-3/4 on Monday.</p>
<p>-- Alpha Industries Inc said it expects a third quarter charge of not more than $0.26 a share to divest its European ceramics manufacturing operations and digital radio subsystem product line.</p>
<p>Alpha shares closed at 7-5/8.</p>
<p>-- ADAC Laboratories said it would discontinue its quarterly dividend of $0.12 a share. Its shares closed at 21-7/8.</p>
</text>
